# {{APP_NAME}} recordings

Recorded scenarios of {{APP_NAME}}, built on Runcast (see
[`.kit/README.md`](.kit/README.md) after setup): each runs as an end-to-end
test or is recorded into a demo video.

## Setup

1. With the Runcast plugin, ask your AI assistant to set up recordings;
   or run the plugin's `skills/runcast-setup/kit/cli.ts setup` yourself. It links `.kit` to the
   kit's runtime (gitignored).
2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` and fill in the account.
3. Start the app ({{BASE_URL}}).
4. `node {{DIR}}/.kit/cli.ts test login`

## Commands

From the repository root, `node {{DIR}}/.kit/cli.ts <command>`:

| Command                    | What                                                |
| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `doctor`                   | What is installed, what is missing                  |
| `test [name]`              | Headless end-to-end test                            |
| `rehearsal [name]`         | The video's pace, headless, not recorded            |
| `video [name]`             | Record, then a picture per step (`--render`: MP4)   |
| `render [name]`            | Render the last capture → `videos/<name>.mp4`       |
| `narration <cmd> <name>`   | Voice-over tools (plan, generate, measure, ...)     |
| `youtube <cmd> [name]`     | Upload a video to YouTube (runcast-publish skill) |

